The review has been written to `docs/reviews/infiltration-deep/infil-deep-03-aim2-coefficients.md`.

**Summary of findings:**

- **5 total findings** (0 critical, 0 high, 2 medium, 3 low)
- **No coefficient errors discovered** that would produce systematic infiltration biases — the HARES implementation passes cross-validation against OCHRE at <0.5% tolerance and the runtime quadrature formula matches EnergyPlus exactly.

The key structural finding is that EnergyPlus doesn't compute AIM-2 coefficients at all (they're user inputs via `ZoneInfiltration:FlowCoefficient`), so direct code-to-code comparison of the coefficient derivation wasn't possible. The two medium findings concern documentation mismatches with Walker & Wilson (1998) source material and a possible flue-exponent refinement in the wind factor formula inherited from OCHRE.
